+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm install` and `pnpm start` to serve the site. After changing the INP
+instrumentation in `src/`, run `pnpm build` to regenerate `assets/inp.js`.
+The generated bundle is committed so the static page works without a build step.
+
+## Diagnose slow interactions
+
+The locally bundled `web-vitals/attribution` library measures INP during real
+interactions. It reports when the page is hidden, including when navigating away.
+No interaction means no INP report; this is not a page-load metric.
+
+Set the `inp-report-endpoint` meta tag in `index.html` to an existing analytics
+collector URL to send reports using `sendBeacon`, with a keepalive fetch fallback.
+The collector must accept JSON in a `text/plain` POST body. This static app does
+not provide a collector. With an empty endpoint, no analytics requests are sent.
+Aggregate the latest `value` per metric `id`, rather than counting repeated reports
+as separate visits. Back/forward cache restores receive a new metric ID.
+
+For local integrations, read `window.inpDiagnostics.latest` or subscribe to
+`window.addEventListener('inp-report', ({ detail }) => { /* consume report */ })`.
+Reports become available after the library reports the metric, typically when
+the tab is hidden. `supported` identifies Event Timing support;
+`scriptAttributionSupported` identifies Long Animation Frames support.
+
+Start with the three durations (all times are milliseconds):
+
+- `inputDelay`: the main thread was busy before event handlers could run.
+- `processingDuration`: event handlers took too long.
+- `presentationDelay`: work after event processing delayed the next paint.
+
+Use `interactionTarget` and `interactionType` to locate the slow interaction.
+When present, `longestScript` identifies the script URL, function, character
+position, overlapping phase, and forced style/layout time. This is a diagnostic
+lead rather than proof that a single function caused the entire delay.
+Additional script, style/layout, and paint totals help explain rendering work.
+Browsers without Long Animation Frames still report INP phases but return
+`longestScript: null`; browsers without Event Timing skip measurement.
+Reports include the page pathname, selector, and script URL, but no input values
+or element text. Review collector configuration for your deployment.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for serialization and transport checks.
